# Hand-written: what a run of the app makes and no one commits.
#
# `Gemfile.lock` IS committed, and is the exception that proves the rule:
# without it CI resolved the gem set afresh on every run, so an upstream
# Rails release could redden the system job with no change in this
# repository. Refresh it deliberately with `bundle update`, never as a
# side effect. Keep `BUNDLED WITH` at the Bundler the Ruby the CI job
# pins ships (3.3 -> 2.5.22): ruby/setup-ruby reads that line and uses
# it, so a lockfile written by a newer Bundler makes the job install one.
/storage/*
/db/schema.rb
/log/*
/tmp/*
/.bundle
